{"assets":[],"contentKind":"statement","contestId":"1827","diagnostics":[],"document":{"children":[{"attrs":{"level":1,"role":"title"},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"F. Copium Permutation"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"time_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"time limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"2 seconds"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"memory_limit"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"memory limit per test"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":"1024 megabytes"}],"kind":"container"},{"attrs":{"role":"body"},"children":[{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"You are given a permutation $$$a_1,a_2,\\ldots,a_n$$$ of the first $$$n$$$ positive integers. A subarray $$$[l,r]$$$ is called "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"copium"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" if we can rearrange it so that it becomes a sequence of consecutive integers, or more formally, if $$$$$$\\max(a_l,a_{l+1},\\ldots,a_r)-\\min(a_l,a_{l+1},\\ldots,a_r)=r-l$$$$$$ For each $$$k$$$ in the range $$$[0,n]$$$, print out the "},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"maximum"}],"kind":"container"},{"kind":"text","text":" number of copium subarrays of $$$a$$$ over all ways of rearranging the last $$$n-k$$$ elements of $$$a$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"input_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Each test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases $$$t$$$ ($$$1 \\le t \\le 10^4$$$). The description of the test cases follows."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The first line of each test case contains a single integer $$$n$$$ ($$$1\\le n\\le 2\\cdot 10^5$$$)."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"The second line of each test case contains $$$n$$$ integers $$$a_1, a_2, \\ldots, a_n$$$ ($$$1 \\le a_i \\le n$$$). It is guaranteed that the given numbers form a permutation of length $$$n$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"It is guaranteed that the sum of $$$n$$$ over all test cases does not exceed $$$2\\cdot 10^5$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"output_specification"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"For each test case print $$$n+1$$$ integers as the answers for each $$$k$$$ in the range $$$[0,n]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"samples"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Example"}],"kind":"heading"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample"},"children":[{"attrs":{"role":"sample_input"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Input"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n5\n5\n5 2 1 4 3\n4\n2 1 4 3\n1\n1\n8\n7 5 8 1 4 2 6 3\n10\n1 4 5 3 7 8 9 2 10 6\n"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"sample_output"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":3},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Output"}],"kind":"heading"},{"kind":"code_block","text":"\n15 15 11 10 9 9 \n10 8 8 7 7 \n1 1 \n36 30 25 19 15 13 12 9 9 \n55 55 41 35 35 25 22 22 19 17 17 \n"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"section"},{"attrs":{"role":"note"},"children":[{"attrs":{"level":2},"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"Note"}],"kind":"heading"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the first test case, the answer permutations for each $$$k$$$ are $$$[1,2,3,4,5]$$$, $$$[5,4,3,2,1]$$$, $$$[5,2,3,4,1]$$$, $$$[5,2,1,3,4]$$$, $$$[5,2,1,4,3]$$$, $$$[5,2,1,4,3]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"},{"children":[{"kind":"text","text":"In the second test case, the answer permutations for each $$$k$$$ are $$$[1,2,3,4]$$$, $$$[2,1,3,4]$$$, $$$[2,1,3,4]$$$, $$$[2,1,4,3]$$$, $$$[2,1,4,3]$$$."}],"kind":"paragraph"}],"kind":"section"}],"kind":"document"},"index":"F","problemCode":"1827F","schema":2,"sourceKind":"html","sourceUrl":"https://codeforces.com/contest/1827/problem/F"}